  "texts": {
    "preamble": "B.Sankar vs The Secretary To Government on 20 July, 2015 Author: D.Hariparanthaman Bench: D.Hariparanthaman In The High Court Of Judicature At Madras Dated : 20.07.2015 Coram The Honourable Mr.Justice D.Hariparanthaman W.P.No.21498 of 2015 1 B.Sankar 2 J.Sakthiumaibalan 3 N.Sathish Kumar 4 L.Subburayalu 5 V.Sugumar 6 P.Kannan 7 R.Sakthivel 8 B.Prabhu 9 S.Roberty Ramesh 10 S.Gnanaprakasam 11 T.Suresh 12 P.Kuppamuthu 13 A.Subramanian 14 K.B.Revathi 15 A.Gunaseelan 16 T.Balaguru 17 V.Veramani 18 P.Perumalsamy 19 A.Balan 20 S.Selvarani 21 S.Martin De Porres 22 S.Prabhu 23 V.Aravind 24 T.Palanimurugan 25 J.Gurusamy 26 P.Gopalakrishnan 27 S.Ramaiah ... Petitioners Vs. 1 The Secretary to Government of Tamilnadu Department of Health Fort St. George Chennai-9 B.Sankar vs The Secretary To Government on 20 July, 2015 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/44285551/ 1 2 The Commissioner of Food Safety No.359 Annasalai Chennai-6 3 The Secretary to Government of Tamilnadu Municipal Administration and Water Supply Department Fort St. George Chennai-9 4 The Director of Public Health and Preventive Medicine No.359 Anna Salai Chennai-6 5 The Commissioner Chennai Corporation Chennai ... Respondents Prayer: Petition filed under Article 226 of the Constitution of India to issue a Writ of Mandamu For Petitioners : Mr.V.Vijay Shankar For Respondents : Mrs.M.E.Rani Selvam for R1 to R4 Additional Government Pleader Mr.S.Saravanan for R5 O R D E R Heard both sides.",
    "facts": "2) In the representation second cited, Food Inspectors of Corporation of Chennai has stated that, out of 62 Food Inspectors in Chennai Corporation 25 have already been selected as Food Safety Officers as per the Food Safety and Standard Act 2006, vide proceedings of the Commissioner, Tamil Nadu Food Safety and Drug Administration Department, Chennai. Now the remaining 37 Food Inspectors of Chennai Corporation have requested the Government to recommend their names to the Department of Tamil Nadu Food Safety and Drug Administration for taking up the post of Food Safety Officers. The Principal Secretary/ Commissioner, Corporation of Chennai has also recommended the above proposal to the Government.",
